ts=2026-08-18T00:00:00Z actor=opencode event=roadmap_created roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Isomorphic world-map baseline planned" notes="Cloudmappr is a standalone project. The active baseline is an MJS D3/TopoJSON world map with five static shards, shared MapSpec/scene construction, Deno canonical SVG/PNG rendering, GitHub/esm.sh delivery, and client export/share support. Pre-rendered SVG land is deferred pending proof."
ts=2026-08-18T00:00:00Z actor=opencode event=roadmap_update roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Generic map-contract migration checklist linked" notes="Added Cloudmappr memory identifying remaining reusable Custom Element, presentation/accessibility, source provenance, label, and deferred SVG-fragment requirements to migrate from prior map research while excluding Corfeed-specific application and actor concerns."
ts=2026-08-18T00:00:00Z actor=opencode event=roadmap_update roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Generic map-contract migration completed" notes="Created and routed governing contracts for the optional Custom Element, presentation/accessibility, artifact provenance, and label behavior. Retained the SVG-fragment proposal as a deferred experiment with receiver and export proof gates."
ts=2026-08-18T00:00:00Z actor=opencode event=ledger_routing_added roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Tiered agent routing and grep-first discovery added" notes="Added AGENTS.md, control.yaml, ledger.yaml, and discovery guidance. Agents now orient through T0-T3 routing, select roadmap sections through grepable hooks, and use Glob/Grep before source reads."
ts=2026-08-18T00:00:00Z actor=opencode event=runtime_baseline_added roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Deno bootstrap and functional baseline recorded" notes="Added root mise.toml with latest Deno and recorded the pure-core, typed-failure, functional lint, and colocated atomic/seam/live test strategy. Candidate npm packages were checked before later workspace adoption."
ts=2026-08-18T00:00:00Z actor=opencode event=functional_tooling_implemented roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Deno functional core tooling verified" notes="Added Deno tasks, pinned functional and ESLint dependencies, core functional primitives, and colocated atomic/seam/live test files. mise run verify passed Deno lint, ESLint, type checking, and four non-live tests; mise run test-live passed the explicit live convention."
ts=2026-08-18T00:00:00Z actor=opencode event=svelte_dependency_added roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Standalone Svelte consumer dependency added" notes="Installed svelte 5.56.9 without SvelteKit and routed the wrapper boundary: map behavior remains in the framework-neutral MJS controller; a future Svelte component only owns lifecycle and prop/event translation."
ts=2026-08-18T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=pages_local_delivery_planned roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Local GitHub Pages build and branch publication routed" notes="Added a ready strategy for locally building, previewing, and publishing static Pages output through a dedicated gh-pages branch without a repository GitHub Actions workflow. The MJS controller, manifest, data-artifact, CDN, esm.sh, and release pipeline remain intentionally undecided."
ts=2026-08-18T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=esm_selected_shard_delivery_routed roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="esm.sh module and selected-shard delivery strategy expanded" notes="Linked a dedicated roadmap decision to the GitHub/esm.sh delivery card. The card now defines explicit per-shard entry points, immutable release identity, candidate MJS-wrapper versus separate-TopoJSON transport, esm.sh transform policy, and external browser/Deno network proof gates."
ts=2026-08-18T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=eight_shard_policy_adopted roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="World delivery policy expanded from five to eight shards" notes="The baseline now uses eager world-basemap plus lazy north-america, south-america, europe, africa, asia, oceania-major, and antarctica TopoJSON artifacts. Atomic-part assignment is versioned and reviewed; the change targets map delivery and bounded render geometry, while broader server-rendering optimization remains future work."
ts=2026-08-18T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=world_generation_toolchain_planned roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Pinned Mapshaper and typed generator boundary recorded" notes="Installed mapshaper 0.7.53 as a development dependency and linked a build-toolchain strategy. The Deno TypeScript generator owns typed eight-shard assignment, validation, manifest, and provenance logic; Mapshaper is a build-only adapter. Every build component requires a narrow contract, and pure primitives remain isolated from filesystem, process, network, and CLI effects."
ts=2026-08-18T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=eight_shard_fixture_proven roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Pinned Mapshaper fixture pipeline emits eight TopoJSON shards" notes="Added a world-artifacts package with typed shard primitives, exact fixture assignment validation, SHA-256 manifest descriptors, and an explicit Deno live test that invokes mapshaper 0.7.53 to emit eight independent land TopoJSON artifacts. mise run verify and mise run test-live pass. This is a fixture proof; real source retrieval, full-world coverage, and release publication remain pending."
ts=2026-08-19T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=artifact_receiver_contract_added roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Pure artifact receiver and local development delivery routed" notes="Added linked receiver and local-development cards. They define immutable receive state and commands, typed store/digest/decoder ports, manifest-only URL safety, local release directory and HTTP route rules, cache ownership, browser/Deno parity, and atomic, seam, and live proof gates."
ts=2026-08-19T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=artifact_receiver_pure_core_implemented roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Pure artifact selection, planning, and reduction implemented" notes="Added the transport-free receiver core with immutable release state, descriptor URL admission, artifact keys, antimeridian-aware manifest selection, load commands, and duplicate-safe reductions. Four atomic receiver tests pass in mise run verify; manifest parsing, transport, digest, and TopoJSON decode ports remain pending."
ts=2026-08-19T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=artifact_receiver_interpreter_proven roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Receiver interpreter verifies digests through injected ports" notes="Added a ResultAsync interpreter over injected validated-manifest, byte-store, digest, and decoder ports. Fake-port seam tests prove planner-ordered load/reduction and that digest mismatch prevents decode and state reduction. Raw manifest parsing and concrete HTTP/filesystem adapters remain pending."
ts=2026-08-19T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=artifact_manifest_parser_proven roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Pure manifest admission validates the eight-shard release" notes="Added parseManifest and safe manifest URL admission to the transport-free receiver. Atomic tests prove valid canonical input plus rejection of incomplete declarations and traversal artifact URLs. The runtime still needs a raw-byte JSON decoder and concrete HTTP/filesystem stores."
ts=2026-08-19T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=artifact_manifest_byte_boundary_proven roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Receiver interprets raw manifest bytes through pure validation" notes="Replaced the validated-manifest store with manifest bytes plus a manifest-decoder port. The interpreter now applies parseManifest before reduceManifest; seam tests continue to prove planner sequencing and digest-before-topology behavior. Concrete JSON, HTTP, and filesystem adapters remain pending."
ts=2026-08-19T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=fixture_manifest_emission_proven roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Mapshaper fixture release emits and validates manifest.json" notes="The fixture generator now writes manifest.json alongside its eight TopoJSON artifacts. The live proof reads it back through parseManifest while retaining the existing eight-shard, eager-basemap, and digest-shape checks. Release-directory layout, real sources, and local adapters remain pending."
ts=2026-08-20T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=isomorphic_fixture_vertical_slice_implemented roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Browser and Deno render one fixture release through shared scene contracts" notes="Added closed MapSpec validation/canonicalization, d3-geo scene/SVG serialization, MJS D3 controller, HTTP and filesystem artifact adapters, constrained local route, local development command, canonical Deno SVG/PNG API with immutable filesystem store, and fixture live proofs for browser HTTP and Deno rendering parity. The reviewed real-world atomic assignment table and source provenance release remain open."
ts=2026-08-20T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=world_atlas_release_gate_implemented roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Real-source release generator requires reviewed atomic assignments" notes="Added pinned World Atlas countries-110m extraction, stable polygon-part splitting, reviewed-table validation, generic Mapshaper artifact generation, and provenance emission. Normal tests prove source part extraction and refusal of unreviewed/incomplete tables. A human-reviewed assignment table is still required before a production world release can be generated."
ts=2026-08-20T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=world_atlas_review_template_generated roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Atomic World Atlas review artifact generated" notes="Added a review-template task and generated build/world-atlas-assignment-review.json with 282 pending part decisions, bounds, and explicitly non-authoritative centroid suggestions. The file cannot be consumed by the release generator until a reviewer creates the approved assignment record."
ts=2026-08-20T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=browser_build_dependency_boundary_hardened roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Browser receiver avoids build-only World Atlas barrel" notes="Changed client and server receiver composition to import only local HTTP/filesystem adapters rather than the world-artifacts barrel. This keeps Mapshaper and World Atlas source/review modules out of the browser artifact graph; verify and live suites pass."
ts=2026-08-20T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=browser_controller_dom_proven roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="MJS controller DOM lifecycle has a permissioned seam proof" notes="Added JSDOM proof for keyed land/marker/label mounting, repeat setSpec root stability, and controller teardown. The DOM runner is included in the explicit live suite because JSDOM reads its own stylesheet package; the complete live suite passes."
ts=2026-08-20T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=viewport_and_10m_source_policy_corrected roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Unclamped viewport policy and 10m release requirement recorded" notes="Analysis found the current proof uses countries-110m, whose 282 polygon parts are unsuitable review material for the 10m release. World Atlas countries-10m has 255 country features and 4,253 polygon parts. Keep eight delivery shards, review country/territory policy plus exceptions, materialize atomic assignments, avoid data-availability clamping, and add prefetch/retention behavior before release."
ts=2026-08-20T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=seeded_partition_proposal_routed roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Seven-seed frontier and hard-corridor shard proposal added" notes="Added a linked ready strategy describing fixed regional seeds, bounded geodesic frontier growth, forbidden geographic corridors, residual eager basemap behavior, 10m review scope, and promotion measurements. It is explicitly a proposal and does not replace the eight-shard policy or approve assignments."
ts=2026-08-20T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=rule_first_partition_contract_routed roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Rule-first geographic exceptions and pure partition core recorded" notes="Added linked strategy and contract cards. The policy is total and explained: named geographic rules and deterministic seed paths precede a residual basemap fallback; any explicit atomic-part exception is release-scoped, justified, and validated. The pure core receives validated facts and produces coverage-proven assignments without filesystem, network, CLI, or publication effects."
ts=2026-08-20T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=ten_metre_policy_emission_decided roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="10m classification, deterministic partition graph, and dissolved coastline emission accepted" notes="The accepted direction uses countries-10m for classification/audit, derives reproducible adjacency and bounded geodesic frontier facts, represents corridors as executable geometry, assigns whole parts, keeps residual land in the eager basemap, and dissolves/re-topologizes each emitted shard to prevent country-border rendering. Generic clustering is not a runtime or build dependency."
ts=2026-08-20T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=ten_metre_partition_candidate_implemented roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="10m rule-first candidate pipeline emits explained dissolved shards" notes="Replaced the 110m manual-table seam with a checked-in 10m seeded-frontier policy, deterministic shared-boundary and sampled geodesic frontier facts, pure assignment resolution, release-scoped exceptions, explained provenance, and Mapshaper dissolve/re-topology emission. Atomic tests and the live 10m eight-shard decode proof pass; performance measurements and production publication remain open."
ts=2026-08-20T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=ocean_polar_island_shards_deferred roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Residual island shard expansion routed as a measured deferred proposal" notes="Recorded observed basemap composition, the incorrect residual assignment of Antarctica part 010:0, candidate Arctic/Southern/Pacific buckets, and the need for coverageBounds[] before dateline-split Pacific delivery. The eight-shard baseline remains active until correctness repairs and comparative measurements justify expansion."
ts=2026-08-20T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=antarctica_basemap_assignment_repaired roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Antarctica mainland leaves eager residual basemap" notes="Added a named force-shard-for-parts policy rule for 010:0, bumped the 10m policy revision, and emitted a new immutable candidate. The policy report and live artifact proof place it in antarctica; world-basemap falls from 2,209,793 to 2,089,976 raw bytes."
ts=2026-08-20T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=southern_ocean_residuals_reassigned roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Southern Ocean residual land moves into existing lazy Antarctica shard" notes="Added the named southern-ocean-land rule below 50 S in the v3 10m policy. The report proves all southern parts now resolve to antarctica, preserving eight descriptors while reducing world-basemap from 2,089,976 to 1,942,319 raw bytes; the live eight-artifact emission proof passes."
ts=2026-08-20T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=ten_metre_promotion_strategy_routed roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="10m candidate promotion and measurement work item detailed" notes="Added a ready roadmap work item and linked strategy covering policy audit, candidate hygiene, real-release browser/Deno receiver parity, canonical size/performance measurements, review comparison against v2, and immutable GitHub/esm.sh handoff. Updated manifest acceptance rules so residual basemap and one-bbox baseline can evolve without conflicting with the deferred island-shard strategy."
ts=2026-08-20T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=remaining_island_shard_implementation_planned roadmap=cloudmappr status=deferred summary="Versioned multi-footprint receiver and staged island-shard plan recorded" notes="The deferred strategy now requires a v1-compatible closed core-plus-optional manifest catalog, pure coverageBounds selection, a second pure residual classifier, report-driven geographic rules instead of ordinary atomic overrides, and trials in order: Arctic then the East/West Pacific pair. Southern Ocean stays in antarctica; Atlantic, Indian, and a separate Southern Ocean artifact need fresh evidence. Promotion compares geometry and delivery work to the v3 control."
ts=2026-08-20T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=island_shard_trials_implemented roadmap=cloudmappr status=deferred summary="v4 Arctic and v5 Arctic/Pacific candidates are generated, parity-proven, and not promoted" notes="Implemented v1-to-v2 manifest coverage normalization, a closed optional artifact catalog, multi-footprint selection, a pure residual classifier with major-land detachment, derived optional coverage, candidate CLI generation, real-release browser/Deno parity, and measurement/comparison commands. Three-run v3 control comparisons reject v4 and v5 for promotion because full-world request/byte cost rises; v3 remains the active eight-shard release."
ts=2026-08-20T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=roadmap_reconciled_after_island_trials roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="Completed candidate measurement and manifest-contract evidence is now reflected in the roadmap" notes="The active artifact contract now distinguishes the required eight-ID baseline from closed optional candidate IDs, and the 10m promotion work records completed three-run measurements. Policy audit, all-scenario real-v3 parity, v2 comparison/review, and publication remain open; v4/v5 candidates remain explicitly not promotable."
ts=2026-08-20T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=coastal_attachment_and_ocean_successors_planned roadmap=cloudmappr status=deferred summary="Detailed next basemap-reduction strategy added" notes="The successor sequence now starts with pure same-source-territory coastal attachment to an already selected major shard, followed by a post-attachment report, Indian candidate, then conditional Atlantic candidate. It records v5 residual diagnostics, forbids ordinary override lists and world-wide footprint collapse, requires bounded footprint compaction proof, keeps Southern Ocean in antarctica, and retains v3 as baseline until measured promotion evidence passes."
ts=2026-08-20T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=coastal_attachment_audit_implemented roadmap=cloudmappr status=deferred summary="Typed provenance and read-only same-territory attachment audit proven" notes="Atomic parts now preserve SourceFeatureId. The pure audit neither changes assignment nor emits artifacts; at a provisional 350 km budget, the real v5 run reports 1,204 residual decisions: 519 attachable, 5 corridor-blocked, 374 without a same-territory major owner, and 306 too distant. Policy application and release measurement remain open."
ts=2026-08-20T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=coastal_attachment_delivery_order_refined roadmap=cloudmappr status=deferred summary="Coastal attachment now gates all remaining optional shard work" notes="The roadmap and governing strategy make reviewed same-territory attachment the only next assignment mutation. Its post-attachment residual report then gates bounded footprint-compaction proof, an Indian candidate, and only conditional Atlantic evaluation. Arctic and Southern Ocean variants are explicitly out of the current sequence; the v5 Arctic/Pacific candidate remains not promotable."
ts=2026-08-20T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=coastal_attachment_v6_candidate_implemented roadmap=cloudmappr status=deferred summary="Pure same-territory coastal attachment is generated and measured as an evidence-only candidate" notes="Added an optional versioned coastalAttachment policy phase before residual classification, explicit coastal-attachment explanations, a post-attachment report, v6 generator task, and atomic proof. The 350 km v6 candidate attaches 519 of 1,204 v5 residual parts, leaving 924 and reducing world-basemap to 369,007 raw bytes. v6 is not promotable: it adds 2,036 full-world raw bytes versus v5 and, versus v3, three requests and 15,314 raw bytes."
ts=2026-08-20T00:00:00Z actor=user event=v6_pan_first_delivery_accepted roadmap=cloudmappr status=active summary="v6 accepted; full-world cost is non-blocking compatibility evidence" notes="Cloudmappr is a pan-first, effectively non-zooming map with no global-map use case. Initial viewport-relevant shards may be delivered in one wrapped payload while preserving individual immutable identities and digests; only pan-induced selections fetch lazily. v6's ordinary-view reductions are accepted, and full-world request/byte measurements no longer veto promotion."
ts=2026-08-20T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=initial_artifact_payload_contract_routed roadmap=cloudmappr status=ready summary="Deno Deploy wrapped initial-payload, cache, and compression contract recorded" notes="Added a linked contract for canonical release-plus-selection pack URLs, binary framing, member digest verification, explicit outer Brotli/gzip negotiation, immutable edge caching, browser per-artifact cache seeding, functional effect boundaries, and production proof gates. esm.sh remains immutable module/artifact delivery, not dynamic pack assembly."
ts=2026-08-20T00:00:00Z actor=codex event=initial_artifact_payload_core_implemented roadmap=cloudmappr status=ready summary="Canonical initial-payload framing and verification core proven" notes="Added format-1 binary framing with a full manifest index, canonical selected-set SHA-256 key, selected-member identity/offset/length checks, and digest verification before cache seeding. Atomic tests cover round trip plus identity and corruption rejection. Deno Deploy compression/edge-cache route and browser cache adapter remain open."
